{
  "id": "model-psychosis",
  "term": "model psychosis",
  "definition": "Model psychosis refers to an experimentally induced psychosis-like state in healthy people used to study possible mechanisms of psychotic experiences. In the source, mescaline is described as being used this way to explore self-disturbances linked to schizophrenia.",
